{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.BringResidueResolvent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.BringResidueResolvent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_at_q_eq_2_cascade","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_at_q_eq_2_cascade","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L236-L251","doc":"**Phase-3 cascade check.**  At `q = 2 : ℚ`, the resolvent\nequation holds concretely at all four downstream pole orders —\ndischarged via the `Fact`-instances above firing the default\n`bringResidueAtOrder_of_pole_nonzero`, then composing with the\nspecialisations `bring_residue_at_T_3_5`, `bring_residue_at_T_2_9`\nand `bring_residue_meson_pair`. No hypothesis required. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instFactNeRatHSubOfNatHMulHShiftHPow_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instFactNeRatHSubOfNatHMulHShiftHPow_3","kind":"instance","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L233-L234","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instFactNeRatHSubOfNatHMulHShiftHPow_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instFactNeRatHSubOfNatHMulHShiftHPow_2","kind":"instance","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L230-L231","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instFactNeRatHSubOfNatHMulHShiftHPow_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instFactNeRatHSubOfNatHMulHShiftHPow_1","kind":"instance","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L227-L228","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instFactNeRatHSubOfNatHMulHShiftHPow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instFactNeRatHSubOfNatHMulHShiftHPow","kind":"instance","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L221-L225","doc":"`Fact`-instance carrying the n=3 pole non-vanishing. Fires the\ndefault `bringResidueAtOrder_of_pole_nonzero` to give a concrete\nsorry-free `BringResidueAtOrder 3 (2 : ℚ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_q_eq_2_pole_nonzero_at_10","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_q_eq_2_pole_nonzero_at_10","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L214-L219","doc":"Phase-3 concrete pole non-vanishing at n = 10, q = 2 : ℚ\n(#1445 p-n averaging color-tube weight `[10]_q`).\n`1 - (3/2) · 2¹⁰ = 1 - 1536 = -1535 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_q_eq_2_pole_nonzero_at_9","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_q_eq_2_pole_nonzero_at_9","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L208-L212","doc":"Phase-3 concrete pole non-vanishing at n = 9, q = 2 : ℚ\n(#1444 α_EM `[9]_q`).  `1 - (3/2) · 2⁹ = 1 - 768 = -767 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_q_eq_2_pole_nonzero_at_4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_q_eq_2_pole_nonzero_at_4","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L202-L206","doc":"Phase-3 concrete pole non-vanishing at n = 4, q = 2 : ℚ\n(meson `[4]_q` index).  `1 - (3/2) · 2⁴ = 1 - 24 = -23 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_q_eq_2_pole_nonzero_at_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_q_eq_2_pole_nonzero_at_3","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L195-L200","doc":"Phase-3 concrete pole non-vanishing at n = 3, q = 2 : ℚ\n(meson `[3]_q` index).  `hShift 2 = 3/2`, so\n`1 - (3/2) · 2³ = 1 - 12 = -11 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bringResidueAtOrder_of_pole_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bringResidueAtOrder_of_pole_nonzero","kind":"instance","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L170-L178","doc":"**Default instance** for the strengthened class: any concrete\n`(n, q)` with the pole non-vanishing hypothesis (carried as a\n`Fact`) discharges `BringResidueAtOrder n q` directly.  Lets\ndownstream code instantiate the class via a non-vanishing fact\nrather than the full §3b-cond axiom-class chain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_subsingleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_subsingleton","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L157-L168","doc":"**Sub-singleton companion.**  The space of field elements equal\nto `canonicalResolvent n q` is a subsingleton — immediate by\ndefinition of equality (no class instance required).\n\nRetained for downstream §3b-cond bookkeeping (the resolvent form\nis unique as a closed-form element of the substrate field). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_meson_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_meson_pair","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L146-L155","doc":"**Specialisation at the meson force-carrier indices 3 and 4** —\n`[3]_q · [4]_q = m_K² / m_π²` from PR #1455.  Each leg satisfies\nits own resolvent equation, jointly carrying the meson GMOR\nfactorisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_at_T_2_9","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_at_T_2_9","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L138-L144","doc":"**Specialisation at α_shift(T(2, 9)) = 9** — the `[9]_q` factor\nin #1444's `1 / α_EM = q · [9]_q · [10]_q + 2/(3π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_at_T_3_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_at_T_3_5","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L129-L136","doc":"**Specialisation at α_shift(T(3, 5)) = 10** — the Bring\ncolor-tube p-n averaging weight from the merged #1445.  Now states\nthe substantive resolvent equation at pole order 10. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_equation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bring_residue_equation","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L110-L127","doc":"**Resolvent equation theorem (Phase-2 substantive content).**\n\nGiven the strengthened Bring residue class with the pole\nnon-vanishing precondition, the canonical resolvent form satisfies\nthe **resolvent equation** $(1 - h_q \\cdot q^n) \\cdot F_n(q) = 1$.\nThis is the algebraic identity that any concrete contour-integral\nor substrate-Bloch-group route must produce — the bridge from\n\"pole order n proved via `prop:alpha-shift-torus-knot`\" to the\nclosed-form resolvent ansatz used downstream (PRs #1444, merged\n#1445, #1455).\n\nSorry-free: proof is `mul_inv_cancel₀ h.pole_nonzero`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:bring-residue-resolvent","label":"prop:bring-residue-resolvent","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringResidueAtOrder.pole_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringResidueAtOrder.pole_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L108-L108","doc":"The pole at order `n` is **non-vanishing**: `1 - h_q · q^n ≠ 0`.\n\nIn a `Field`, `canonicalResolvent n q = (1 - h_q · q^n)⁻¹` is\nalways a field element (`x⁻¹` is total, with `0⁻¹ = 0`).  The\ncontent of this precondition is that the denominator is\nnon-zero, so the resolvent behaves as a *genuine reciprocal*\nand the resolvent equation can be discharged via\n`mul_inv_cancel₀`.\n\n**Strengthened 2026-05-30 (Phase 2 of the §3b-cond template):**\nthe previous existential field `∃ r : R, r = canonicalResolvent n q`\nwas trivially provable via `⟨canonicalResolvent n q, rfl⟩` —\nthe literal-rfl loophole that #1460 closed for\n`BringZeroModeBlochClass`.  The strengthened field requires\nthe **pole non-vanishing condition** that any concrete\ncontour-integral route (Mathlib `CircleIntegral` or substrate\n`BlochSuslin`) must establish first; once the pole is\nnon-zero, the resolvent equation\n`(1 - h_q · q^n) · (1 / (1 - h_q · q^n)) = 1` follows by\n`mul_inv_cancel₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringResidueAtOrder.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringResidueAtOrder.mk","kind":"ctor","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringResidueAtOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringResidueAtOrder","kind":"class","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L63-L108","doc":"**Class: Bring residue at pole order `n` evaluated at substrate\nparameter `q`.**\n\nAxiomatises the contour-integral / Schwarz-integral on Bring's\nsurface around the simple pole of order `n` of σ on the\nrelevant torus knot (T(p, k) with α_shift(p, k) = n).  The\nsole field `pole_nonzero` records the **non-vanishing of the\ndenominator** `1 - h_q · q^n`, which is the precondition for the\ncanonical resolvent form to behave as a genuine reciprocal\n(rather than the total-but-degenerate `0⁻¹ = 0` branch of `Field`).\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-cond: closes the resolvent-form question by\n*naming* the pole non-vanishing as the substantive contour-\nintegral output; closing the class instance for a specific\n(n, q) requires either:\n- the Mathlib analytic-residue machinery\n  (`Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.RemovableSingularity`,\n   `Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.CircleIntegral`), OR\n- an algebraic identification via the substrate's\n  Bloch-Suslin framework\n  (`em-coupling-bring-zero-mode.lean`'s\n   `BringZeroModeBlochClass`).\n\nClosing the class is queued as a Mathlib-import follow-up. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonicalResolvent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonicalResolvent","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L54-L61","doc":"The **canonical resolvent form** at pole order `n`:\n`F_n(q) := 1 / (1 - h_q · q^n)`.  This is the target closed\nform whose derivation from the Bring residue integral is the\nopen math.  Defined here as the substrate ansatz against which\na `BringResidueAtOrder n q` class instance is matched. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hShift","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-residue-resolvent.lean#L49-L52","doc":"The substrate bar shift `h_q = q - q⁻¹`.  Bar-invariant under\n`q ↔ q⁻¹` (with a sign flip).  Standard from the Iwahori-Hecke\nrelation `(σ - q)(σ + q⁻¹) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}